<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">People's Revolutionary Government (Grenada)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1979–1983</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The People's Revolutionary Government was the socialist government of Grenada formed after the New Jewel Movement under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maurice-bishop">Maurice Bishop</a> overthrew <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eric-gairy">Eric Gairy</a> on 13 March 1979. It built close ties with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuba">Cuba</a> and began an international airport at Point Salines. In October 1983 a split within its leadership led to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">Bishop</a>'s execution, followed by the United States-led invasion of Grenada.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/peoples-revolutionary-government-grenada.jpg" alt="People's Revolutionary Government (Grenada)" width="320" height="192" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: See file history below for details. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Grenada.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
